module bankr-ias-local-rules.local-rules

// The Bankr. S.D. Iowa court has no local bankruptcy rules: "Effective
// August 4, 2003, this court's local rules were abolished. Attorneys and
// pro se parties shall consult the Federal Rules of Bankruptcy Procedure"
// (the court's Bankruptcy Rules page, sources/bankr-ias). Every period,
// page limit, filing and service rule in the court is therefore lit/frbp's
// (and the Code's), and none is declared or restated here. The court's
// standing and general orders, forms and chapter 13 trustee procedures are
// not vendored; any period they state is a hole in the corpus.
start case-pending

state case-pending: "Case pending under the Federal Rules of Bankruptcy Procedure" by applicant cite ?("Rule 1001 of the Federal Rules of Bankruptcy Procedure (scope and short title): sources/frbp.txt does not vendor Rules 1001 through 1006")
{
  note "The court abolished its local rules effective August 4, 2003; attorneys and pro se parties consult the FRBP (the court's Bankruptcy Rules page). The case runs on lit/frbp's periods."
  edge-case-pending-frbp "No local rule: the FRBP govern" -> governed {
    authority cite "FRBP 9029(a)"
  }
}

terminal governed: "Matter governed by the FRBP: the case continues under lit/frbp" outcome [procedural] cite "FRBP 9029(a)"
{
  note "A district court may authorize its bankruptcy judges to make local rules (FRBP 9029(a)); this court has none since August 4, 2003."
}
